# Tokens for demo.http. Copy to .env and fill in the values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored, so this file must never contain a real token. Nothing in this project reads
# .env on its own: the Worker gets its token from .dev.vars, and only the VS Code REST Client
# extension reads this one, through an explicit `{{$dotenv name}}` reference in a .http file.
#
# localToken: the value of EVENTS_API_TOKEN in your .dev.vars. Both must be the same string or the
# local requests in demo.http get 401 while everything else local keeps working.
# prodToken: the production secret. `npx wrangler secret list` names it but never shows the value,
# so take it from wherever you kept it after running `npx wrangler secret put EVENTS_API_TOKEN`.
#
# The two are independent on purpose: a token leaked from one machine must not open production.
#
# Generate a local one with:  node -e "console.log(crypto.randomUUID())"

localToken=local-dev-token
prodToken=prod-token-here
